## THE TEXTS (ASCII; you build them from your readings, freeze them to `.tools/b987/out/texts987.json` and the plan to `.tools/b987/scratch/plan.json` BEFORE the first write; the shape below is approved by Tuesday's read-whole, the figures are yours, each asserted by program to `runs/assert-table-R97.txt` with a planted wrong figure reported DIFFERENT)
**Jira text rule (binding, as B873):** no person's name, no client or sample-client name, no decision-card slug, no price, no amount of money, no percent sign, no digit-dot-digit (no version number), no backtick, no email, ASCII only; the words Tuesday, Wednesday, Friday and HP 0 times; PRs are written "MPS #n". Gate work numbers (for example "gate B157") are allowed, as in the earlier comments. Run `scan610.py scan()` on ALL payloads BEFORE the first write (selftest first: the planted control fires all kinds); the fence has no edit.
- Comment, bold-led paragraphs, one ADF paragraph each, SHORT (the landing comment is cited by id and not repeated): **BLUF.** "Done-when met; moved to Done." or "Recorded; not moved." then one sentence: MPS #n, squash <40 hex>, merged <UTC> (<AEDT> by program), re-read from the API on the write day, and an ancestor of code main <sha8>. **Review.** the gate line as the gate wrote it (tier 1) or "tier 2: reviewed at source by the coordinator; no QA gate" (tier 2, only if `TIER2-ATTEST` is YES), plus the landing comment id. **Done-when, clause by clause.** from the 4a table, MET or NOT MET each, with what is not done named plainly; a red `ci` push run on the squash named with its run id when there is one. **Hosted.** "The squash is an ancestor of the build the project records as hosted (relayed, not probed by this pass)." **Status.** "Moved to Done by the coordinator's instruction; the move rests on that instruction and on these checks, not on a ruling of the product owner." or "Not moved: <clause>." Closing line: "Source: records pass B987, 2026-10-31. [B987]" (the skip marker).
- No sentence says deployed, live or complete as the pass's own claim; no duration or difference is computed in Jira text.

